  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Breaking. Authorization outcomes that retrying the same request will not change are now one exception family under AuthClientException: the new SignInRefusedException, with StatusCode, for a refused sign-in, replacing UnauthorizedAccessException and the HttpRequestException other refusals threw; the new SessionNotRenewableException for a client built from an AuthResponse whose refresh token is missing or refused, replacing InvalidOperationException; and InvalidAuthResponseException. A server that fails rather than refuses still throws HttpRequestException, now with StatusCode set, and a refresh answered that way keeps the refresh token. Calls waiting on authorization share one failed sign-in or refresh attempt instead of each retrying it, and ForceAuthorizeAsync, which the send methods call after a 401, returns without a new attempt when another call's attempt succeeded while it waited. Messages are rewritten. See https://github.com/AdamTovatt/easy-reasy/blob/auth-client-v2.0.0/EasyReasy.Auth.Client/README.md#from-180",
